---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StepsStrip from '../components/StepsStrip.astro';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Why does the result come out as a JPG?',
    a: 'Because a PNG that stays a PNG can only shrink a little: PNG saving is lossless, so the only honest levers are re-saving the same pixels (a few percent, sometimes nothing) or making the picture smaller. A door with a hard KB limit cannot be met that way. So this page lands your exact target the way that actually works, as a JPG, and says so here and at the tray before you run, never after.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How exact is the result?',
    a: 'On a normal photo, this search landed within about half a percent of the target at 200, 100, 50 and 20 KB. The page searches quality and, when quality alone has no setting close enough, the dimensions too, and it shows you the exact final size and how far it sits from your target.',
  },
  {
    q: 'My PNG must stay a PNG. What are my honest options?',
    a: 'Two. Make it smaller in pixels: the resize image page cuts the dimensions, which is where most of a PNG\'s weight lives. Or convert it on purpose, knowing the trade: the PNG to JPG page paints any see-through parts over a colour you pick and writes the lighter format. What this workshop will not do is hand you a slightly re-saved PNG and call the job done when it misses your limit.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where does my picture go?',
    a: 'Nowhere. It is decoded, re-encoded and offered back to you inside this page. Nothing is uploaded.',
  },
];
const faqJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
});
const howToJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HowTo',
  name: "How to compress a PNG to an exact KB",
  step: [
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 1, name: "Pick the PNG picture", text: "Drop a PNG picture on the tray, or click to pick one. It stays on this device. Another picture kind is pointed at the compress image page." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 2, name: "Pick the target", text: "Choose a preset target or type your own target in KB. The result is a JPG at that target: the page states this before the run, because a PNG that stays a PNG cannot honestly land a hard KB target." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 3, name: "Compress to the target", text: "Press 'Compress to the target'. The page decodes your PNG and runs a search: it encodes at different quality settings, watches the sizes, and closes in on your target; on hard pictures it adjusts the dimensions too." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 4, name: "Download the JPG", text: "The achieved size and its distance from your target are shown on the result." },
  ],
});
const targets = [200, 100, 50];
---

<Base title="Compress PNG to an exact KB, free, in your browser · Benchzy" description="Shrink a PNG picture to 200 KB, 100 KB, 50 KB or an exact size you pick, with the work done inside your browser. The page states plainly, before the run, that the result is a JPG at your target. No upload, no account.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">Image tools · PNG</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black mt-2">Compress PNG</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        A PNG picture, and a door that wants it under a size limit. The plain truth first,
        because it decides everything on this page: a PNG that stays a PNG shrinks very
        little, since PNG saving throws nothing away. Sometimes converting beats
        compressing. So this page lands your exact KB target as a JPG, in your browser,
        with nothing uploaded, and says so before you run, never after. If the file must
        stay a PNG, your honest levers are <a class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-deep" href="/resize-image/">smaller dimensions</a>
        or a deliberate <a class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-deep" href="/png-to-jpg/">PNG to JPG conversion</a>.
        Other picture kinds are on the <a class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-deep" href="/compress-image/">compress image page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ticket mt-6 p-5 sm:p-7" id="ci-tool" data-lock-format="png">
      <div id="ci-tray" class="tray p-6 text-center cursor-pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Pick a PNG picture">
        <p class="font-display text-xl font-bold">Drop a PNG picture on the tray, or click to pick one</p>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-soft mt-2">PNG in · JPG out at your target · it stays on this device</p>
        <input id="ci-file" type="file" accept="image/png,.png" class="hidden" />
      </div>
      <p class="file-loaded hidden" data-loaded-for="ci-file" role="status"></p>

      <div class="grid gap-6 mt-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_320px]">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">Target size</h2>
          <div id="ci-targets" class="flex gap-2 mt-3 flex-wrap">
            {targets.map((kb) => (
              <button type="button" class="chip" data-kb={kb} aria-pressed="false">{kb} KB</button>
            ))}
          </div>
          <label class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft block mt-5" for="ci-custom">Or your own target (KB)</label>
          <input id="ci-custom" type="number" min="5" max="20000" step="5" class="mt-2 border border-ink bg-ticket px-3 py-2 font-mono w-40" />
          <img id="ci-preview" alt="The compressed result" class="hidden w-full border border-line bg-paper-deep object-contain max-h-72 mt-6" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">File spec</h2>
          <dl id="ci-spec" class="mt-2">
            <div class="spec-row"><dt>file</dt><dd>none picked yet</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="action-note">
            The result is a JPG at your target, not a smaller PNG: that is stated here,
            before the run, on purpose. A PNG that must stay a PNG shrinks by
            <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/resize-image/">dimensions</a>, not by a quality search.
          </p>
          <button id="ci-run" class="btn-primary w-full mt-5" type="button" disabled>Compress to the target</button>
          <p id="ci-status" class="font-mono text-sm mt-4 leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite">Pick a PNG picture to begin.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="ci-result" class="receipt hidden mt-8">
        <div class="tear pt-5 flex items-center gap-4 flex-wrap">
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">Result</h2>
          <span class="stamp" id="ci-stamp">Done on your device</span>
        </div>
        <p id="ci-achieved" class="mt-3 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl"></p>
        <a id="ci-download" class="btn-primary inline-block no-underline mt-3" href="#" download>Download the photo (JPG)</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <StepsStrip who="For a PNG screenshot or graphic that must fit an exact KB limit on a form, a listing, or a marketplace upload, where the door accepts a JPG." steps={[{ n: '01', t: 'Pick the PNG picture' }, { n: '02', t: 'Pick the target' }, { n: '03', t: 'Download the JPG at the target' }]} />

    <section class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">How it works</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The page decodes your PNG and runs the same search as the compress image tool: it
          encodes at different quality settings, watches the sizes, and closes in on your
          target. On hard pictures, quality alone has no setting that lands close (the
          steps jump over the window), so the search then adjusts the dimensions too. That
          combined search is the shipping method here; on the hardest test photo we have,
          it landed within about a third of a percent of the target.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Honest limits</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The trade is on the table before you run: the output is a JPG, because a hard KB
          target cannot be honestly met while staying PNG: lossless saving only re-packs
          the same pixels. PNG shrinks less than JPG by design, and sometimes converting
          beats compressing, which is why the
          <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/png-to-jpg/">PNG to JPG page</a> exists
          as its own door with its own warning about see-through parts. Very small targets
          also mean a softer or smaller picture; the result line always states the quality
          and dimensions used. This door takes PNG only: that is its framing, and the tray
          says so when another kind of picture arrives.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
        {faq.map((f) => (
          <article class="ticket-soft p-5">
            <h3 class="font-bold">{f.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mt-1">{f.a}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqJson}></script>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={howToJson}></script>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/compress-image.js';
  </script>
</Base>
